<article class="help-article p-4">
    <header class="help-article-header mb-4">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined help-article-icon">dashboard</span>
        <h1 class="help-article-title">Navigating the Editor</h1>
        <p class="help-article-lead">
            The Editor is the main workspace for shaping a project model, switching between projects,
            editing selected objects, and reviewing the model as a table or graph.
        </p>
    </header>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Editor layout</h2>
    <ul class="help-list">
        <li><strong>Navigator</strong> &mdash; the left pane groups model objects into Entities, Composite Types, Fetch Request, and Configurations.</li>
        <li><strong>Content</strong> &mdash; the center pane shows the selected entity's properties, index elements, composite elements, fetch predicate, or graph view.</li>
        <li><strong>Inspector</strong> &mdash; the right pane edits the selected object and exposes type-specific options.</li>
        <li><strong>Breadcrumb</strong> &mdash; the bottom bar shows the current project, model, and selected object path.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Toolbar controls</h2>
    <p>
        Use the project switcher to jump between recent projects. The segmented control switches between
        the table-style editor and the graph view. The panel buttons show or hide the Navigator and Inspector.
    </p>

    <div class="help-callout">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined">menu</span>
        <div>
            <strong>The main menu follows your selection.</strong>
            Entity property actions are enabled only after selecting an entity. Remove is enabled only
            after selecting an object that can be removed.
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Next steps</h2>
    <p>
        Start with <a class="help-link" href="#entities" data-help-anchor="entities">entities</a>, then add
        <a class="help-link" href="#attributes" data-help-anchor="attributes">attributes</a> and
        <a class="help-link" href="#relationships" data-help-anchor="relationships">relationships</a>.
    </p>
</article>
